# Claude Code harness repo -- SECRETS-SAFE ALLOWLIST.
#
# A ~/.claude directory holds OAuth credentials (.credentials.json), session
# transcripts under projects/ (which can contain pasted secrets), plugin caches,
# and assorted runtime state. Default-ignore EVERYTHING and opt in only curated,
# non-secret harness *source*, so this layout is safe even if it is ever used
# as a live ~/.claude. Never convert this to a denylist.

# 1. Ignore every top-level entry...
/*

# 2. ...then opt specific harness source back in.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/skills/
!/hooks/
!/lessons/
!/agents/
!/bin/
# settings.json is hook wiring + permissions + plugin flags. Constraint: its
# env block must stay secret-free (use OS env vars, never values here).
!/settings.json
# reflections/ mixes source with runtime capture (session-log.jsonl, deltas,
# backups) -- re-include the dir, then opt in ONLY .py/.md source.
!/reflections/
reflections/*
!reflections/*.py
!reflections/*.md

# 3. Within allowed trees, track SOURCE only -- never runtime run-artifacts/outputs
#    (these can capture pasted secrets, e.g. memory-synthesizer/runs/.../agent-outputs).
skills/**/runs/
skills/**/agent-outputs/
skills/**/.cache/
skills/**/output/
skills/**/outputs/

# 4. Defense-in-depth: never track secrets/caches even inside allowed trees.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.key
**/*.pem
**/.credentials*
**/node_modules/
**/*.log
